  "settingsFormulaGuideTitle": "GPS & GPA Formula Guide",
  "settingsFormulaGuideSubtitle": "Explanation of grade calculation and retakes",
  "formulaGuideBody": "1. Semester GPS is historical: Σ(weight × credits) / Σ credits of all entries in that semester (including E grades and retakes).\n\n2. GPA: Σ(weight × credits) / Σ credits using one effective entry per course group (highest grade by default, or latest grade).\n\n3. Grade E always requires a retake (not passed). Before retaking, E is included in the GPA denominator (weight 0). After retaking, the new grade replaces E in GPA while historical Semester GPS remains unchanged.\n\n4. Completed Credits and Completed Courses count each course group whose effective entry passes (≥ minimum passing grade).",
